applies to
>> DTLS or not. There is the one reference in the intro to DTLS, but =
it's not in
>> the abstract, nor anywhere else. Assuming that the Sec. 1 reference =
is not some
>> sort of artifact, the document would benefit from a liberal =
sprinkling of
>> 's/TLS/(D)TLS' (but this would not apply to every instance)
>>=20
